---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="dalemberts-paradox"
  lead="The ideal flow has no wake. The real flow does."
>
  <SvgFigure
    name="dalembert-flows"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg"
    viewBox="0 0 400 310"
    title="Symmetric ideal flow compared with separated real flow"
    desc="Above, smooth streamlines bend equally around the front and back of a stationary round body in an ideal frictionless flow. Below, flow moving left to right separates around the body, leaving a softly shaded red wake region and a small eddy behind it. The figure is schematic, not a measured flow field."
  >
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="17" font-weight="700">
      <text x="12" y="21">
        Ideal flow: front and back match
      </text>
      <text x="12" y="177">
        Real flow: separation and a wake
      </text>
    </g>
    <!-- Both panels have one unobtrusive left-to-right flow arrow. -->
    <g
      fill="none"
      stroke={series.blue}
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
    >
      <path d="M20 36 H62 m-6 -5 6 5 -6 5" />
      <path d="M20 193 H62 m-6 -5 6 5 -6 5" />
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke={series.blue} stroke-width="2">
      <path d="M12 48 H388" />
      <path d="M12 79 C106 79 123 61 200 61 S294 79 388 79" />
      <path d="M12 127 C106 127 123 145 200 145 S294 127 388 127" />
      <path d="M12 158 H388" />
      <!-- Streamlines pass around the body, then separate downstream. -->
      <path d="M12 224 C112 224 124 205 190 205 C219 205 237 215 259 221 C310 217 351 221 388 224" />
      <path d="M12 282 C112 282 124 301 190 301 C219 301 237 291 259 285 C310 289 351 285 388 282" />
    </g>
    <!-- One subdued wake region, rather than overlapping dashed boundaries. -->
    <path
      d="M228 238 C275 230 324 232 388 239 L388 267 C324 274 275 276 228 268 Z"
      fill={series.red}
      fill-opacity=".15"
    />
    <g fill={series.gold} fill-opacity=".25" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="2">
      <circle cx="200" cy="103" r="30" />
      <circle cx="200" cy="253" r="30" />
    </g>
    <path
      d="M267 252 C280 241 300 243 305 253 C312 269 288 272 282 259"
      fill="none"
      stroke={series.red}
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
    />
  </SvgFigure>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Without viscosity the idealised steady flow has front-back symmetry and predicts zero drag.
    In real fluids, viscosity matters near the surface and the flow can separate, leaving a
    low-pressure wake that creates drag. Schematic, not to scale.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
